               # 🧠 Stack & Heap in JavaScript

> **Quick idea:**
> **Stack = execution + variables/references**
> **Heap = dynamically allocated objects/data**

---

## 1. 🏗️ Big Picture

```text
                    JAVASCRIPT MEMORY
                           │
              ┌────────────┴────────────┐
              │                         │
           📚 STACK                  🗄️ HEAP
              │                         │
      ┌───────┼────────┐          ┌─────┼─────────┐
      │       │        │          │     │         │
   Primitive  Function  Reference  Object Array  Function
    values     calls     values             │
      │                            Complex / dynamic data
      │
   number
   string
   boolean
   null
   undefined
   symbol
   bigint
```

> ⚠️ **Important:** This is a simplified mental model. JavaScript does not require engines to physically implement memory exactly this way.

