# 3. 🗄️ HEAP

The **heap** is used for dynamically allocated data such as objects and arrays.

```text
                    HEAP
        ┌──────────────────────────┐
        │                          │
        │   {                      │
        │      name: "John",       │
        │      age: 25             │
        │   }                      │
        │                          │
        │   [10, 20, 30]           │
        │                          │
        │   function (...) {...}   │
        │                          │
        │   Map / Set / Date ...   │
        │                          │
        └──────────────────────────┘
```

Example:

```js
const user = {
    name: "John",
    age: 25
};

const numbers = [10, 20, 30];
```

Simplified memory model:

```text
             STACK                         HEAP

        ┌──────────────┐
        │ user ────────┼──────────────┐
        ├──────────────┤              │
        │ numbers ─────┼─────────┐    │
        └──────────────┘          │    │
                                  │    │
                                  ↓    ↓

                          ┌──────────────────┐
                          │ {                │
                          │   name: "John"   │
                          │   age: 25        │
                          │ }                │
                          └──────────────────┘

                          ┌──────────────────┐
                          │ [10, 20, 30]     │
                          └──────────────────┘
```

