# 8. 💥 Stack Overflow

If functions keep calling themselves without stopping:

```js
function hello() {
    hello();
}

hello();
```

The stack keeps growing:

```text
┌─────────────────┐
│ hello()         │
├─────────────────┤
│ hello()         │
├─────────────────┤
│ hello()         │
├─────────────────┤
│ hello()         │
├─────────────────┤
│ hello()         │
├─────────────────┤
│ hello()         │
├─────────────────┤
│      ...        │
├─────────────────┤
│ Global Context  │
└─────────────────┘
        ↓
   💥 STACK OVERFLOW
```

Because the call stack has a limited amount of memory.

