# 9. 🗑️ Garbage Collection

JavaScript automatically manages memory using **garbage collection**.

Example:

```js
let user = {
    name: "John"
};

user = null;
```

Initially:

```text
STACK                         HEAP

user ─────────────────────→ { name: "John" }
```

After:

```js
user = null;
```

```text
STACK                         HEAP

user → null                  { name: "John" }
                                  ↑
                                  │
                              no reference
```

The object is now **unreachable**.

The garbage collector can eventually reclaim that memory.

```text
Object unreachable
       ↓
Eligible for garbage collection
       ↓
Garbage Collector
       ↓
Memory can be reclaimed
```

> ⚠️ "Garbage collected immediately" is not guaranteed. The JavaScript engine decides when collection happens.

