# 11. ⚡ Quick Comparison

| Feature           | Stack                                                   | Heap                                                        |
| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |
| Main purpose      | Execution state / call stack                            | Dynamically allocated data                                  |
| Function calls    | ✅                                                       | Function objects may reside in heap                         |
| Objects           | Reference held here; object storage is engine-dependent | Commonly stored here                                        |
| Arrays            | Reference held here                                     | Commonly stored here                                        |
| Speed             | Very fast access                                        | Generally more flexible, but allocation/access details vary |
| Memory management | Stack frames are removed as calls return                | Garbage collector manages reachable/unreachable objects     |
| Structure         | LIFO call stack                                         | No LIFO requirement                                         |
| Size              | Limited                                                 | Typically much larger                                       |
| Example           | `let x = 10`                                            | `{ name: "John" }`                                          |

